KZ3 patch 1096 (SPU pass 71): direct hops between lifted SPU functions, and a memo for spu_lookup.

Every cross-function transfer in lifted SPU code set the pending trampoline and returned to the enclosing drain
loop, which ran its per-hop hooks and called the target; a computed branch (bi rX that is not a return) went
through the full resolver spu_indirect_branch and spu_lookup, which walks a hash chain holding every image
registered at that LS address (5.4 entries on average for KZ3's 106 images). Software-pipelined SPU loops close
with a computed `bi` (rX = selb(head, exit, cond)), so the audio mixer's hot loops paid a trampoline return, the
drain hooks, the resolver and the chain walk on every iteration: ~20 % of the LoPrio SPU thread in K2 (spu round
70 profile: spu_drain_call_body 7.7, spu_lookup 5.6, spu_indirect_branch 4.2, launch check 3.1 %).

Now (needs a guaranteed tail call: clang or GCC >= 15 musttail; otherwise the old path is compiled):
- static transfers emit SPU_HOP(ctx, A, F): when the drain's hooks would only do bookkeeping (no lockstep, no
  launch diagnostics, no stack-reset entry that could match, no pending enabled interrupt) the lifted code does
  that bookkeeping itself (recent-pc ring, step count, drain_ret_pc) and tail-calls F; else the trampoline as before;
- computed transfers emit SPU_IB_HOP: spu_ib_direct() returns what the resolver would dispatch to when all it would
  do is dispatch (every early path is excluded by state, see its comment), else the trampoline to the resolver;
- ctx->hop_ret_pc holds the innermost call bracket's return pc (lifted brsl/bisl and spu_drain_call_full set and
  restore it), so a computed transfer to that address still goes to the drain, which returns there;
- spu_lookup keeps exact (addr, image) hits in a 16 K-slot memo (one 64-bit word each; the registry is append-only
  and a lookup returns the first match in registration order, so a hit never changes); misses and wildcard
  answers take the walk as before.
KZ3_SPU_HOP=0 = old dispatch; dispatch diagnostic switches (SPU_TAILRET, SPU_JOBTRACE, SPU_JOBEXEC, SPU_POLLTRACE,
SPU_IBCOV, YDKJ_POLTRACE, LBP_HLE_JOBDONE, SPU_PCHIST, KZ3_PMEND_IB) also select it. KZ3_HOP_STATS=1 prints `[hop-stats]` every 10 s: direct computed hops, the fallbacks by reason, resolver calls.
Needs a relift (tools/spu/lift_spu.sh). Upstream candidate.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): ours (SPU_HOP / SPU_IB_HOP) over upstream SPU_DIRECT in the lifter; both context fields.

